course: dictionary
lesson: 15481
title: Stretching: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the sentence tells you which one to use. Stretching is a good example: it can be about your body, about something you pull, about land, or about trying harder.
explain: «Sam did ten minutes of stretching before the football match.» Here stretching is about your body. You reach and pull your muscles gently so they become longer and ready to move.
explain: «The elastic band kept stretching until it snapped.» Here stretching means pulling something so it gets longer. Think of a rubber band: pull it and it stretches.
explain: «The fields were stretching all the way to the hills.» Here stretching means spreading over a distance. Ask yourself what word would fit, then try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
fact: Stretching means making your body, or a part of it, longer, such as reaching your arms and legs out.
fact: Stretching something means pulling it so it gets longer or wider, like a rubber band.
fact: Stretching can also mean spreading over a distance or time: «The road was stretching for miles.»
fact: Stretching yourself means doing something harder than usual so that you learn more.
fact: In PE, stretch gently to warm up and help prevent injuries. Never bounce when you stretch.
exercise: «Sam did ten minutes of stretching before the football match.» What does stretching mean here? | Sleeping in the changing room | Running very fast around the pitch | *Reaching and pulling your muscles gently to get them ready
exercise: «The elastic band kept stretching until it snapped.» What is happening to the band? | Getting shorter and thicker | *Getting longer as it is pulled | Changing colour in the sun
exercise: Ana says, «The fields were stretching all the way to the hills.» What does stretching mean? | Getting smaller and closer | Jumping up and down | *Spreading over a long distance
test: «The cat gave a long, lazy stretching after its nap.» What is the cat doing? | Hiding under the sofa | Running out of the room | *Making its body longer by reaching out its legs
test: Mr Patel says, «Learning this hard maths is stretching for me.» What does stretching mean? | *Doing something harder than usual to learn more | Going to sleep early | Pulling the paper until it tears
exam: «Her goal was stretching, but she trained every day to reach it.» What does stretching mean? | Made of rubber | *Hard and demanding | Easy and quick | Round and smooth
